{
  "summary": "The current `ShieldsSiteState.covering` implementation uses `canonicalHost` on stored entries, which performs IDNA conversion (e.g., 'BÜCHER.example' -> 'xn--bcher-kva.example'). However, the native `DomainOption` parser rejects non-ASCII characters via `RemoveInvalidDomainStrings`. This creates a mismatch where a legacy Unicode entry might 'match' a current host in the UI/logic but would be stripped by the actual filter engine. I propose restricting `covering` to only match entries that are already ASCII-compatible (allowing uppercase) to ensure the 'saved exception' actually exists in the filter engine, without rewriting legacy data.",
  "architecture_observations": [
    "`ShieldsSiteState.canonicalHost` performs IDNA conversion, widening the scope of what it considers a valid host.",
    "`DomainOption::RemoveInvalidDomainStrings` strictly enforces a whitelist of ASCII characters, effectively rejecting Unicode/IDN entries.",
    "The `covering` method currently applies `canonicalHost` to stored entries, causing a mismatch between logical matching and actual filter application.",
    "Existing architecture preserves original entries to avoid unauthorized rewrites."
  ],
  "proposed_changes": [
    {
      "file": "components/adblock/android/java/src/org/chromium/components/adblock/ShieldsSiteState.java",
      "change": "Modify `covering` to avoid calling `canonicalHost` on stored entries. Instead, check if the entry is ASCII-compatible (allowing uppercase) and then use `canonicalHost` for the comparison logic, or simply ensure the entry itself doesn't contain non-ASCII characters before treating it as a valid domain match. Specifically, replace `String domain = canonicalHost(entry);` with a check that ensures `entry` is valid ASCII (ignoring case) to prevent false matches for Unicode entries that `DomainOption` would reject."
    }
  ],
  "patch": "--- a/components/adblock/android/java/src/org/chromium/components/adblock/ShieldsSiteState.java\n+++ b/components/adblock/android/java/src/org/chromium/components/adblock/ShieldsSiteState.java\n@@ -41,8 +41,13 @@\n         String canonical = canonicalHost(host);\n         if (canonical == null) return matching;\n         for (String entry : domains) {\n-            String domain = canonicalHost(entry);\n-            if (domain != null && (canonical.equals(domain) || canonical.endsWith(\".\" + domain))) {\n+            // Only match entries that are already ASCII-compatible to avoid false claims\n+            // for Unicode entries that DomainOption would reject.\n+            boolean isAscii = true;\n+            for (int i = 0; i < entry.length(); i++) {\n+                if (entry.charAt(i) > 127) { isAscii = false; break; }\n+            }\n+            if (isAscii) {\n+                String domain = canonicalHost(entry);\n+                if (domain != null && (canonical.equals(domain) || canonical.endsWith(\".\" + domain))) {\n+                    matching.add(entry);\n+                }\n+            }\n         }\n         return matching;\n     }",
  "risks": [
    "Restricting to ASCII might prevent users from seeing 'saved' status for legacy Unicode entries, even if they technically match the punycode host, though they are functionally useless in the current filter engine."
  ],
  "tests": [
    "Update `idnCaseAndFinalDotCanonicalizeWithoutWideningScope` to assert that 'BÜCHER.example' is NOT returned by `covering` because it is non-ASCII.",
    "Add a test case ensuring 'xn--bcher-kva.example' (the ASCII version) IS returned by `covering` for the same host."
  ]
}

